    "description": "``FPM`` stands for FastCGI Process Manager. It is a PHP FastCGI implementation.\n\nInstead of nesting PHP in the web server, ``php-fpm`` makes PHP a server by itself. The web server then delegates the work to the PHP server. The advantage is to lower the memory footprint of PHP and the web server, and the whole of them both. It helps with stability, by keeping the two processes separated.",
